# Qt GUI Rules

## Separation of concerns
Page and widget classes (`MonitoringPage`, `DashboardPage`, `SettingsPage`, all widgets) must contain **only** presentation logic.
Business logic belongs in service classes under `src/services/`.

## Cross-thread signals
All signals that cross from a worker thread to the GUI thread must use `Qt::QueuedConnection`:

```cpp
// ❌ BAD — default connection from non-Qt thread is unsafe
connect(worker, &Worker::done, this, &Widget::onDone);

// ✅ GOOD
connect(worker, &Worker::done, this, &Widget::onDone, Qt::QueuedConnection);
```

## QSettings keys
Declare all `QSettings` keys as `constexpr` string literals in a dedicated constants header, never as inline string literals scattered through the code:

```cpp
// ❌ BAD
settings.setValue("serialPort", port);

// ✅ GOOD
constexpr auto kSettingsSerialPort = "serialPort";
settings.setValue(kSettingsSerialPort, port);
```

## Qt resource paths
Never construct Qt resource paths (`:/...`) as runtime-built strings.
Use compile-time string literals or `Q_INIT_RESOURCE` only.
